  "name": "dbx 2151 VCA, datasheet application with AN103 offset nulling and a resistive control network (validation circuit)",
  "description": "THAT 2150-series Fig. 3 for the 2151: 10 uF + 20k into IN, pin 5 through 2.7k to -15 V (AN103 Fig. 3 value with its 10k 'DC offset nulling' resistor from the control port to pin 5), SYM pin 4 through 51 ohms to GND, Ec+ pin 2 at GND, OUT into an op-amp with 20k || 47p. Ec- is driven by a 2 Hz, 0.1 V control swing through 100 ohms with 10k to GND (about -12 to +21 dB with the 10k to pin 5 pulling the node down 28 mV), so the control node is a divider loaded by the 10k to pin 5 and by the core's base currents (a second instance with core beta 100). Both outputs are compared.",
  "sources": [
    { "title": "THAT Corporation, 2150 Series IC Voltage-Controlled Amplifiers data sheet rev. 10/25/96 (Figs. 3, 6)", "url": "https://thatcorp.com/datashts/THAT_2150-Series_Datasheet.pdf" },
    { "title": "dbx Application Note 103, The dbx 2150 Voltage Controlled Amplifier (sections I.D, I.E, II.E, Fig. 3)", "url": "https://gyraf.dk/schematics/dbx2150vca_AN.pdf" }
  ],
  "io": { "input": "in", "output": "out" },
  "oversampling": 2,
